/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Johnson.BiaugmentedTruncatedCube.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 47`, `matAt x 38` and `(x 56, x 57)` are a weak fit of `Johnson.BiaugmentedTruncatedCube.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem johnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Johnson.BiaugmentedTruncatedCube.polyhedron Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.S N 47 38 56 := by
  rw [Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.len_eq Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.sqrt_spec (by decide +kernel)) Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.par_ok Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.zs_eq Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.weak_ok Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.poly_eq Pose.JohnsonBiaugmentedTruncatedCube.ok

end Nieuwland.Polyhedra
